\section{Changes since the first draft}

\subsection{Hypotheses}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*, itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{Split:} the four hypotheses became eight, each testing one claim. Two were later dropped, and the remaining six were renumbered H1–H6 (the earlier H8 is now H4, and H7 is now H6).
\item \textbf{Dropped:} not sampling purely for commercial releases (from original H4), because the problem evidence already covers it, and saving samples in the cloud (from original H3), because Sample Browser saves sections online either way.
\item \textbf{Moved:} the criteria came out of the hypothesis text and into the table below, with the same 60\% threshold for all of them.
\item \textbf{Original H1 $\rightarrow$ H1:} “structural goals” became “search goals”, and the part about abandoning tracks was dropped.
\item \textbf{Original H2 $\rightarrow$ H2 + H6:} objective categories over mood and texture tags (H2), and finding better samples by following what they’ve already heard (H6), which came from the berrypicking part.
\item \textbf{Original H3 $\rightarrow$ H3 + H5:} keeping track of which part of a saved song they wanted and why (H3), and making tags and timestamps public (H5, which now carries the pivot trigger).
\item \textbf{Original H4 $\rightarrow$ H4:} preferring unlicensed full songs over paid libraries. “Commercial loop fatigue” became “commercial sample-pack overuse”.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Questions}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*, itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{New:} “Why there?” at the end of Q9.
\item \textbf{New:} a booking questionnaire (F1–F13) that screens candidates, covers the background questions before the call, and decides which blocks each person gets.
\item \textbf{Reworded:} Q8 asks about the last time they needed another sample to go with one they had, instead of whether that is easier.
\item \textbf{Reworded:} 8a asks about the last time they picked a sound because of its label, instead of what they would prefer.
\item \textbf{Reworded:} 9a asks about the last time they went back to a saved song, instead of assuming they come back to it.
\item \textbf{Reworded:} 10a asks whether their online saves are public and whether they wanted credit for a find, instead of whether they would share tagged sections in a tool that doesn’t exist yet.
\item \textbf{Retagged:} Q5 and 5a now also count toward H6, Q7 and Q8 moved from H2 to H6, and Q10, 10a and 10b moved from H3 to H5. Q2 is now background only.
\item \textbf{Moved:} Q10 and its follow-ups into their own block, Block 6: Sharing.
\item \textbf{Added:} interviewer notes under 4a, Q7, 9a and 10a, and notes on which blocks each person gets.
\end{itemize}

