\textbf{Who to book}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*, itemsep=2pt]
\item Not working a full-time job in music production (F4), and used songs, not only packs, as a sample source in the last 6 months (F5: YouTube, Samplette or sampledigging.online, Vinyl/CDs, Spotify or SoundCloud). Don’t require “mostly songs”: people who mainly use packs keep H4 testable.
\item Aim for at least half who save songs in YouTube or Spotify playlists (F7), so H3 has enough answers.
\item Don’t say in the recruiting post which answers get someone booked.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{How to structure the video call interview:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*, itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{Block 1:} use their F1–F5 answers as a quick warm-up instead of asking again.
\item \textbf{Q7:} only if they type searches (F6).
\item \textbf{Block 5:} only if they save songs or samples (F7). Only people who save songs count toward H3.
\item \textbf{Block 6:} everyone. It decides community catalog or personal workspace, so it needs every answer.
\item \textbf{20 minutes (F8):} Blocks 3 and 6.
\item \textbf{30 minutes:} skip Q8, and skip Q6 if Q5’s story already showed how they scan.
\item \textbf{45 minutes:} everything that applies.
\end{itemize}

\section{Interview questions:}
The questions run from background to the problem hypotheses, then the solution ones; the tag before each shows which hypothesis its answer counts toward.

\subsection{Block 1: Background and screening}
\emph{If they filled in the booking questionnaire, use F1–F5 as a quick warm-up instead of asking these again.}

\textbf{1.} [BK] “How would you describe the main genres of music you make, and what inspires your production style?”

\textbf{2.} [BK] “Do you currently release music under an alias, collaborate with artists, or make beats primarily for personal enjoyment, practice, or underground communities?”

\textbf{3.} [Screening] “When making a track, how much do you rely on sampling existing recordings versus composing from scratch with virtual instruments (VSTs) or hardware? Roughly how many samples did you use on your last sampled track, and why did you choose them?”

\subsection{Block 2: Where they get samples (H4)}
\textbf{4.} [H4] “Do you mostly use curated, royalty-free sample libraries (like Splice or Looperman), or do you prefer sampling directly from original full-length songs (on YouTube, Samplette, Tracklib, vinyl)?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{4a.} [H4] “What makes you choose one over the other?” \emph{Read the options only if they’re stuck:} “Is it convenience, cost, sound uniqueness/fatigue, or something else?”
\item \textbf{4b.} [H4] “Which free or paid tools/sites do you use most often to find samples? Has sample licensing/copyright ever been an issue for the music you make, or does it not affect your releases?”
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Block 3: Searching inside songs (H1)}
\textbf{5.} [H1, H6] “Think about the last specific time you searched for a sample inside full-length songs online. What kind of sound or musical part were you looking for, and how long did you spend searching before you felt you spent enough time?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{5a.} [H1, H6] “Roughly how many tracks did you click through and preview before you found one you actually used?”
\end{itemize}

\textbf{6.} [H1] “When you click on an unfamiliar song on YouTube or Samplette, how do you actually scan through the track to find the exact 4-to-8 bar section you want?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{6a.} [H1] “Have you recently found a song where you liked the instrumentation in one section, but ended up skipping it because it wasn’t usable as a sample? What ruined that section for you (e.g., vocals/drums overlapping, different time signature, poor quality mastering, etc.)?”
\item \textbf{6b.} [H1] “Do you specifically hunt for clean, isolated sections in a song (like an intro, break, or solo), or do you use AI stem separation in your DAW on any part of the song? Why one over the other?”
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Block 4: Describing sounds and tags (H6, H2)}
\textcolor{condition}{\textbf{IF F6 ANSWERED “TYPING IN SEARCH”}} \textbf{7.} [H6] “What was the last sound you searched for using text keywords or category filters, and how did you describe it? How often do you find a good sample from a single text search query?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{7a.} [H2] “When browsing platforms that use tags or filters (like Splice, Tracklib, Samplette, or RYM), which categories do you actually trust and rely on (e.g., instruments, BPM, song sections), and which tags do you avoid or find confusing/inaccurate (e.g., mood or texture words)?”
\end{itemize}

\textbf{8.} [H6] “Think of the last time you needed another sample to go with one you already had. How did you go about finding it? Did anything about the first sample guide where you looked?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{8a.} [H2] “Think of the last time you picked a sound or a song because of how it was labelled: a mood, a genre, or an instrument. Did it match what you expected once you heard it?”
\end{itemize}

\subsection{\texorpdfstring{\textcolor{condition}{IF F7 ANSWERED 1-3}}{IF F7 ANSWERED 1-3} Block 5: Saving samples (H3)}
\textbf{9.} [H3] “Do you keep a personal library, playlist, or folder where you save songs or samples you discovered for future projects? Do you store them locally on your drive or online (e.g., YouTube playlists, bookmarks, sites like chop-stop / sampledigging)? Why there?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{9a.} [H3] “How do you categorize what you save? The last time you went back to a song you’d saved to sample later, did you remember which part you wanted, and why you saved it? How did you find it?” \emph{If they never go back to saved songs:} What stops you from going back to them?
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Block 6: Sharing (H5)}
\emph{Ask everyone.}

\textbf{10.} [H5] “Have you ever shared your sample finds, digging playlists, or song sources with other producers, or do you prefer to keep your found songs private?”
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{10a.} [H5] “If you save samples online, like in a YouTube playlist, is it public or private? Why? If you shared a sample with someone, did you want to be credited for finding the sample?” \emph{Skip the first part if everything is on their drive.}
\item \textbf{10b.} [H5] (Gatekeeping probe) “Has there ever been a time when you found a great, rare sample and deliberately kept the song title secret until your project was finished or released to prevent others from flipping it first?”
\end{itemize}

